(6737285, 1007505, 96574, '<td valign="top">The location is beautiful.<br/>I do think the tones make the shot as a whole, flat. nothing really anchors the eye except for maybe the bright side of the sky.  Like mentioned, maybe if the road were dodged a bit and a crop that had a bit more land and less sky.  I think it would be nicer if the sunset would be a bit more saturated too.</td>', 'The location is beautiful.I do think the tones make the shot as a whole, flat. nothing really anchors the eye except for maybe the bright side of the sky.  Like mentioned, maybe if the road were dodged a bit and a crop that had a bit more land and less sky.  I think it would be nicer if the sunset would be a bit more saturated too.', '2012-04-09 15:06:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6737298, 1007505, 65319, '<td valign="top">This landscape fills my eyes with gorgeous potential.  The sky has appetizing drama and well-exposed clouds and sun provide beautiful filtered light.  I''m beginning to fall in love.  The road wends perfectly through the hills and stands out as a anchor to this image.  I like the divided horizon in the middle because you break a rule here!  Go for it!  However, I gave this image a 6 because the green color of the hills reminded me of the color of over-cooked asparagus.  And, there''s only one place for anything the color of mushy vegetables...</td>', 'This landscape fills my eyes with gorgeous potential.  The sky has appetizing drama and well-exposed clouds and sun provide beautiful filtered light.  I''m beginning to fall in love.  The road wends perfectly through the hills and stands out as a anchor to this image.  I like the divided horizon in the middle because you break a rule here!  Go for it!  However, I gave this image a 6 because the green color of the hills reminded me of the color of over-cooked asparagus.  And, there''s only one place for anything the color of mushy vegetables...', '2012-04-09 15:28:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(6737312, 1007436, 112739, '<td valign="top">Wow Rian! This image is full of solitude and beauty. Just wonderful!</td>', 'Wow Rian! This image is full of solitude and beauty. Just wonderful!', '2012-04-09 16:01:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(6737318, 1007505, 16106, '<td valign="top">This is a lovely subject, but not processed to do well here at DPC. When looking into the sun you often get this sort of low contrast haziness you have here, but being true to what you saw only gets brownie points, not a good score. With a muted color pallet, you have two choices, crank up the vibrance, or convert to B&amp;W.<br/> <br/>The main subject is that windy road, but it gets a bit lost in the image, had you zoomed in and rotated the format to portrait so the road filled more of the frame and the sky was no more than the top third (it is a nice, but not spectacular sky) then the image would have the "pop" that is rewarded at DPC.<br/> <br/>There was a thread on Graduated Neutral Density filters earlier in the week, and this image could be a poster child of a "without" image that a GND would have helped, that bright sky steals so much of the magic of the rolling landscape where all the tones have been squished down into the right side of the histogram, so they lack dynamic range and color information.</td>', 'This is a lovely subject, but not processed to do well here at DPC. When looking into the sun you often get this sort of low contrast haziness you have here, but being true to what you saw only gets brownie points, not a good score. With a muted color pallet, you have two choices, crank up the vibrance, or convert to B&W. The main subject is that windy road, but it gets a bit lost in the image, had you zoomed in and rotated the format to portrait so the road filled more of the frame and the sky was no more than the top third (it is a nice, but not spectacular sky) then the image would have the "pop" that is rewarded at DPC. There was a thread on Graduated Neutral Density filters earlier in the week, and this image could be a poster child of a "without" image that a GND would have helped, that bright sky steals so much of the magic of the rolling landscape where all the tones have been squished down into the right side of the histogram, so they lack dynamic range and color information.', '2012-04-09 16:07:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6737340, 1007521, 135756, '<td valign="top">Wow! I don''t know what happened here, going over the results and seeing worse and worse pics and then this pops out! I had to check where it ranked because it deserved to be way higher. Awesome capture!</td>', 'Wow! I don''t know what happened here, going over the results and seeing worse and worse pics and then this pops out! I had to check where it ranked because it deserved to be way higher. Awesome capture!', '2012-04-09 16:29:30.000000', NULL, 0),
